Sonic paddled out with her surfboard, caught the perfect wave, and glode powerfully back to the shore. The cool breeze felt good against her board shorts. This rhythmic activity had been edifying her since she began it. She turned back to the water when a sight in the sky caught her eye. She stood there, gazing upwards: a fiery flying car and bike many miles above, plunging down like two eagles in a death spiral, a trail of evil-looking smoke behind them. 
